VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  Framework-vs-LambdaCDM, on the data in hand: UNDECIDED and prior-dominated -- the same conclusion the committed fork likelihood reached
  among the framework's own laws.  The test that decides it is specific: the BTFR / deep-MOND zero-point of massive discs at z ~ 2.5,
  where the framework's flat law predicts 0.00 dex and LambdaCDM's emergent halo scale predicts +0.3 to +0.4 dex; one clean point at
  +/-0.15 dex decides at 20:1.  Existing clean points (Big Wheel z=3.25 at +0.06 +/- 0.22; McGaugh+24 null) lean flat but are too coarse.
  Both ways: a measured rise on that arm kills the framework's flat law (and standard MOND with it); a measured constancy forces the
  LambdaCDM fabric change of crispy_fabric_prediction_2026.py.

